    sha256: 9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea
  body: "# Effective date of a supersession\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe supersession process separately
    requires a decision about the date from which the new decision takes effect.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n\
    A date of change, date of notification, application date and legal effective date are not interchangeable. The
    initial batch has not modelled the chapter’s benefit-specific effective-date rules.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 04050, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-relevant-change-of-circumstances
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The change-of-circumstances passage distinguishes the time a change happened from whether it
      can support supersession, including disallowance qualifications.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0017
      quote: "04102 For the purposes of supersession a relevant change of circumstance is a change which happens\n\
        after the original decision had effect and which has a relevance to the award of benefit. A decision\ndisallowing
        a benefit cannot be superseded if there is a change of circumstances from a date after the\n\ndecision had
        effect. The claimant must make a fresh claim 1. But see DMG 04103 for an exception to this\ngeneral rule.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                            1 s 8(2)(b);
        R(A) 4/81"
      locator: DMG 04102
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0017
      quote: "04103 The claim continues to exist until it is decided1. A new claim may not be required where\n\n\
        \n1. a claim is disallowed and\n\n\n2. a change occurs after the date of claim but before the claim was
        decided and\n\n\n3. the claimant notifies the change within the time limits (see DMG 04201 -04211).\n\n\n\
        Where the effect of the change is that entitlement would begin before the date of the disallowance (or\n\
        for AA and DLA, the qualifying period would begin before the date of the disallowance), the decision can\n\
        be superseded for a relevant change of circumstances. The effective date rules apply in the normal way.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                            1 SS Act
        98, s 8(2)(a)"
      locator: DMG 04103
